(Regression test for bug #68: the three spellings that ALREADY worked, kept
 working. These are what isolated the defect - a bare list literal and a
 quoted list name both parse as expression parts too (bug #44 added Print's
 List arm for them), and a mixed list's `first` happened to be a number, so
 the static guess was right. Only the element read was wrong, so a fix that
 broke any of these would have traded one defect for another.

 Acceptance: the neighbours render exactly as bug #44 left them.)

a list called nested is [1, [2, 3], "four"].
a list called 'the deep one' is [4, [5, 6]].
a map called person is {"name": "Ada"}.

Print "lit {[1, 2]}".
Print "quoted {'the deep one'}".
Print "first {nested's first}".
Print "whole {nested}".
Print "map {person}".
